{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:f6cd5be372e0cf33","name":"Kissai","source":{"id":"source:reference-f6cd5be372e0cf33","title":"Kissai","revision":25911,"timestamp":"2025-01-05T02:18:10Z","sha256":"290b8182b2ae815ca1a3bd9bd698c7e9bdb1ab02adabb4e7da01f60a2d1882d1","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25911","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Kissai&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-f6cd5be372e0cf33","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Massassi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Massassi","referenceId":"reference:5369acf6589c1958"}," and Kissai are two subspecies of the original Sith race of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Korriban"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Korriban","referenceId":"reference:e5de27f696051005"},". The Kissai are the priests and spiritual leaders who indoctrinate their comrades in the teaching of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Kissai are just as ruthless as the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Massassi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Massassi","referenceId":"reference:5369acf6589c1958"},", but they are more intelligent and observant. Their strict cultural standards demand that they serve their masters well, a trait instilled in them by the Dark Jedi who first enslaved their Species. When the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Massassi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Massassi","referenceId":"reference:5369acf6589c1958"}," and Kissai flee ",{"tag":"a","children":["Korriban"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Korriban","referenceId":"reference:e5de27f696051005"}," (well before the arrival of the eventual Sith Lords) to resettle on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ziost"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ziost?action=edit&redlink=1"},", the Kissai oversee the rebuilding efforts.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Kissai serve The Sith directly, but the Sith Lord ",{"tag":"a","children":["Naga Sadow"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Naga_Sadow?action=edit&redlink=1"}," has other ideas for the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Massassi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Massassi","referenceId":"reference:5369acf6589c1958"}," caste. The Kissai are largely left on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ziost"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ziost?action=edit&redlink=1"}," as the servants of other Sith Lords, but Sadow uses ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Alchemy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Alchemy"}]}," to transform the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Massassi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Massassi","referenceId":"reference:5369acf6589c1958"}," into his hulking, brutish soldiers. His ",{"tag":"a","children":["Massassi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Massassi","referenceId":"reference:5369acf6589c1958"}," crews labor under his command on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin 4"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin_4","referenceId":"reference:5f008a1b1f754b64"},", building temples and providing the means for him to hide his ship and practice his dark arts. After Sadow's death, they become a primitive, tribal society worshiping one of Sadow's creations as a dark god.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Kissai Characteristics"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Personality:"]}," Kissai are loyal and capable allies who prefer to work with others, making them excellent aides and assistants. They respond well to instruction and are adaptable despite great adversity.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Physical Description:"]}," Kissai have glowing yellow eyes and crimson hides. They are humanoid with distinctly sharp, predatory features. A typical Kissai stands 1.8 meters tall and weighs 90 kilograms.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Age Groups"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Age_Groups"},":"]}," Kissai age at the following stages:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHILD\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["YOUNG ADULT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["ADULT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MIDDLE AGE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["OLD\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["VENERABLE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1-10 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["11-15 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["16-30 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["31-42 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["43-59 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["60+ Years\n"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Homeworld:"]}," The ancient Sith world of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Korriban"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Korriban","referenceId":"reference:e5de27f696051005"},", resettled later to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ziost"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ziost?action=edit&redlink=1"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Kissai speak and read the ancient language of the Sith, and most tend to learn Basic to better serve their Sith masters.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Example Names:"]}," Drophan, Kalgrath, Uburluh, Zythmnr.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Adventurers:"]}," Most beings in the galaxy would not recognize a Kissai at first glance, though their unique appearance tends to draws attention to themselves. Kissai do not become ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi","referenceId":"reference:0b0e48747027a29d"}," during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic_Era"},", and instead most adventurous Kissai become ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nobles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nobles"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrels"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrels"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Kissai Species Traits"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Kissai share the following Species Traits:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Ability Modifiers:"]}," All Kissai receive a +2 bonus to their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Charisma"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Charisma"},", but suffer a -2 penalty to their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wisdom"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wisdom"},". Kissai are charming and pleasant, but their devotion to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," blinds them to the suffering that follows."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Medium Size:"]}," As medium creatures, Kissai have no special bonuses or penalties due to their size."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Kissai have a base speed of 6 squares."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Inspired:"]}," Kissai make the best use of any inspiration or information provided to them. Whenever a Kissai receives a morale or insight bonus from any source, the bonus increases by +1."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Warrior's Awareness:"]}," Kissai grow up in a violent and warlike society, so they constantly watch for threats. Once per encounter as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reaction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reaction"},", a Kissai can gain the benefit of the ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Uncanny Dodge I"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Uncanny_Dodge_I"}]}," and ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Uncanny Dodge II"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Uncanny_Dodge_II"}]}," Talents until the beginning of the Kissai's next turn."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weapon Familiarity:"]}," Kissai treat the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Massassi Lanvarok"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Massassi_Lanvarok","referenceId":"reference:7af6e37093a959d7"}," as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Simple Weapon (Ranged)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Simple_Weapon_(Ranged)"}," instead of an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapon (Ranged)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapon_(Ranged)"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Automatic Languages:"]}," All Kissai can speak, read, and write both Basic and Sith."]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
